	(text "PROJECT-SPECIFIC CAPTURE BLOCKS\n- U2 is the Pimoroni inky EEPROM on I2C1 at 0x50.\n- J3/J4 are Qw/ST on the same I2C1 bus; address 0x50 is reserved.\n- SW1-SW4 are rear buttons using software pull-ups.\n- J5 is a virtual DESPI-C73 8-pin host-net block; the real 50-pin FPC/boost block is still pending."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 124.46 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "30f5e016-7530-5263-8f16-492f11c9c68a")
	)
	(text "Additional pin functions:\nhttps://pinout.xyz/"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 179.07 180.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "36e2c557-2c2a-4fba-9b6f-1167ab8ec281")
	)
	(text "TODO: Replace J5 with the real DESPI-C73-derived 50-pin FPC and boost/test network after visual pin-by-pin verification of reference/despi-c73-schematic-20220728.pdf."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 124.46 215.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "4591b7c5-92e9-55c3-a5af-e18707103c90")
	)
	(text "ID_SD and ID_SC PINS:\nThese pins are reserved for HAT ID EEPROM.\n\nAt boot time this I2C interface will be\ninterrogated to look for an EEPROM\nthat identifes the attached board and\nallows automagic setup of the GPIOs\n(and optionally, Linux drivers).\n\nBridging JP1 enables HAT+ ID EEPROM write protection.\n\nDO NOT USE these pins for anything other\nthan attaching an I2C ID EEPROM. Leave\nunconnected if ID EEPROM not required."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.51 193.04 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8714082a-55fe-4a29-9d48-99ae1ef73073")
	)
